{
  "schema": "ornith-optimized-vllm-recapture-classes/1",
  "what": "Every decode-trace re-capture each server logged, bucketed by how many programs had been compiled since the capture. The physical-block class (roughly 100-300 programs) is the one the 16-block warm-up removes. The residual buckets decompose into three classes, measured in prefill_program_keys.json, prefill_chunk_offsets.json and slot_program_keys.json: the logical-length class (3 aligned, 7-13 non-aligned per new length; the 56 at max_num_seqs=32 is 8 new lengths x 7), the chunk-offset class of a multi-chunk prompt (6 per new offset; the 19 bucket is 2 new offsets = 12 plus 7 for one new tail length), and the slot-remap class (~2 programs per row index not moved before: 4/4/8 at widths 2/4/8 on an 8-slot probe, 20 at width 10, 64 at a first width-32 remap on both trees, 32 on a server whose earlier widths had already moved half its rows). Prefilling into a slot compiles nothing, so multi-request prefill is not a class. README section 3.3.",
